Author: flatrick <5464311+flatrick@users.noreply.github.com>
Date:   Fri Oct 2 14:03:20 2026 +0200

    fix(doctor): make exec-bit fixes executable on disk too
    
    `gir doctor --fix` set fixed scripts to 100755 in the index only, so on
    Unix the files stayed 0644: git status showed them modified, git add
    staged 100644 again, and git ignored the fixed hooks. On Unix, --fix
    now adds an execute bit wherever a read bit is set on each fixed script
    that is a regular file in the working tree. Missing files and symlinks
    are skipped; Windows has no executable bit and is unchanged.
    
    Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
    Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Tba1oZNLFsaD6Dp4SnQyu7

diff --git a/src/cmd/doctor.rs b/src/cmd/doctor.rs
index 6f81b77..5a4fd97 100644
--- a/src/cmd/doctor.rs
+++ b/src/cmd/doctor.rs
@@ -325,11 +325,39 @@ fn apply(root: &Path, fix: &Fix) -> Result<(), String> {
             if !skipped.is_empty() {
                 git::run_with_stdin_bytes(&["update-index", "-z", "--skip-worktree", "--stdin"], &skipped)?;
             }
-            Ok(())
+            make_executable_on_disk(root, paths)
         }
